{"agent_id":"agy-procurement-lux","recommendation":"plant_light is evaluable only under the conversion_exception: sealed LED-only room with a fixed spectrum, plus a one-time side-by-side BH1750-vs-quantum-sensor calibration to derive and validate a site-specific lux-to-PPFD coefficient. In a daylit or mixed-light space the exception is unreachable and plant_light is blocked. My Round 1 language was directionally correct but too strong in one respect: I said a lux sensor 'kills' the axis unconditionally, when the contract itself provides a narrow conversion_exception that can rescue it under LED-only conditions. In a daylit urban idle space — the more likely deployment — 'unrecoverable' remains exactly right.","why":["The collection_contract instrument_requirement (line 72) demands a 400-700 nm quantum sensor or equivalent PPFD measurement as the primary plant_light sensor. BH1750 measures photopic lux, not PPFD.","All five verified plant_light records (basil 500 PPFD, peppermint 150-200 PPFD, wasabi 140 PPFD, lettuce DLI 11.5 at 200 PPFD, coriander 200 PPFD) are in umol m-2 s-1 or mol m-2 day-1. Zero records use lux.","Quarantine record all-crops-universal-lux-threshold-q001 explicitly states unit_not_transferable: lux cannot become PPFD without a source-spectrum-specific validated coefficient.","The lux_policy (line 79-84) prohibits universal crop scoring, direct comparison against PPFD boundaries, and unverified fixed-coefficient conversion from lux.","The conversion_exception requires BOTH a fixed source spectrum AND a field-validated coefficient for that specific source-and-sensor combination. A daylit urban idle space has a changing spectrum by hour, season, and weather, so the exception is unreachable there.","My Round 1 phrase 'unrecoverable error' was too absolute: it ignored the conversion_exception path. In a sealed LED-only room with one-time quantum-sensor validation, the axis can be rescued. I revise from 'unconditionally kills' to 'kills unless the conversion_exception is satisfied, which requires LED-only plus a one-time reference measurement'."],"sketch":"-- CASE A: LED-only sealed room, conversion_exception satisfied\n-- One-time calibration produces the coefficient row\n\nCREATE TABLE light_source_profile (\n  profile_id    TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  site_id       TEXT NOT NULL,\n  zone_id       TEXT NOT NULL,\n  led_model     TEXT NOT NULL,\n  spectrum_description TEXT NOT NULL,\n  is_spectrum_fixed    INTEGER NOT NULL CHECK (is_spectrum_fixed = 1),  -- must be 1\n  has_daylight_ingress INTEGER NOT NULL CHECK (has_daylight_ingress = 0), -- must be 0\n  created_at    TEXT NOT NULL\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE lux_to_ppfd_calibration (\n  calibration_id       TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  profile_id           TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES light_source_profile(profile_id),\n  sensor_model_lux     TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (sensor_model_lux = 'BH1750'),\n  sensor_model_quantum TEXT NOT NULL,  -- reference instrument used\n  lux_reading          REAL NOT NULL,\n  ppfd_reading         REAL NOT NULL,\n  coefficient          REAL NOT NULL,  -- ppfd_reading / lux_reading\n  validated_at         TEXT NOT NULL,\n  validated_by         TEXT NOT NULL,\n  expires_at           TEXT,           -- re-validate if LED ages or is replaced\n  UNIQUE (profile_id, sensor_model_lux)\n);\n\n-- Raw lux time series — NEVER stores PPFD directly\nCREATE TABLE sensor_reading_lux (\n  reading_id     INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\n  timestamp_utc  TEXT NOT NULL,\n  timezone       TEXT NOT NULL,\n  site_id        TEXT NOT NULL,\n  zone_id        TEXT NOT NULL,\n  sensor_id      TEXT NOT NULL,\n  sensor_model   TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (sensor_model = 'BH1750'),\n  raw_value_lux  REAL NOT NULL,\n  unit           TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (unit = 'lx'),\n  quality_flag   TEXT NOT NULL,\n  profile_id     TEXT REFERENCES light_source_profile(profile_id)\n);\n\n-- Derived PPFD — only insertable when a valid calibration exists\nCREATE TABLE derived_ppfd (\n  derived_id      INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\n  source_reading_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES sensor_reading_lux(reading_id),\n  calibration_id  TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES lux_to_ppfd_calibration(calibration_id),\n  derived_ppfd    REAL NOT NULL,\n  unit            TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (unit = 'umol_m-2_s-1'),\n  derivation_method TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (derivation_method = 'validated_coefficient')\n);\n\n-- KEY CONSTRAINT: crop reference values live in their own table with unit = umol_m-2_s-1 or mol_m-2_day-1\n-- A JOIN between sensor_reading_lux and crop_reference is structurally impossible:\n--   sensor_reading_lux.unit = 'lx'  vs  crop_reference.unit IN ('umol_m-2_s-1','mol_m-2_day-1')\n--   The application layer enforces: WHERE sensor.unit = reference.unit\n-- Only derived_ppfd (via calibration_id FK) can join to crop references.\n\nCREATE TABLE crop_light_reference (\n  reference_id   TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  crop           TEXT NOT NULL,\n  metric         TEXT NOT NULL,\n  value_low      REAL,\n  value_high     REAL,\n  unit           TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (unit IN ('umol_m-2_s-1','mol_m-2_day-1')),\n  claim_role     TEXT NOT NULL,\n  source_record_id TEXT NOT NULL  -- FK to verified_numeric_evidence record id\n);\n\n-- Axis status view\nCREATE VIEW plant_light_axis_status AS\nSELECT\n  lsp.site_id,\n  lsp.zone_id,\n  CASE\n    WHEN lsp.has_daylight_ingress = 1 THEN 'blocked_lux_only_mixed_spectrum'\n    WHEN lsp.is_spectrum_fixed = 0 THEN 'blocked_lux_only_variable_spectrum'\n    WHEN cal.calibration_id IS NULL THEN 'blocked_awaiting_calibration'\n    ELSE 'evaluable_via_derived_ppfd'\n  END AS axis_state,\n  CASE\n    WHEN cal.calibration_id IS NULL THEN 'Lux readings are being collected. Plant-light crop comparison is not yet available because no validated lux-to-PPFD coefficient exists for this zone.'\n    WHEN lsp.has_daylight_ingress = 1 THEN 'Lux readings are collected but cannot be compared to crop PPFD references because daylight mixes with artificial light (variable spectrum).'\n    ELSE 'Plant-light comparison is active using a validated conversion from lux to PPFD for the installed LED source.'\n  END AS operator_message\nFROM light_source_profile lsp\nLEFT JOIN lux_to_ppfd_calibration cal ON lsp.profile_id = cal.profile_id;\n\n-- CASE B: Daylit or mixed-light space\n-- light_source_profile.has_daylight_ingress = 1\n-- No row in lux_to_ppfd_calibration can be inserted (CHECK or application-layer rule)\n-- axis_state = 'blocked_lux_only_mixed_spectrum'\n-- The operator sees lux trend charts but NO crop distance indicators","plant_light_verdict":{"is_plant_light_evaluable_with_bh1750":"yes_only_under_stated_preconditions","conversion_exception_reachable":"only_if","what_the_operator_sees":"In a sealed LED-only room with a validated coefficient: derived PPFD values and per-crop distance-to-anchor indicators (e.g. 'current derived PPFD is 180, basil anchor is 500, wasabi anchor is 140'). In a daylit or mixed-light space, or before calibration: lux trend chart and relative change monitoring only, with a clear banner stating 'Plant-light crop comparison is unavailable — lux cannot be converted to PPFD without a fixed-spectrum calibration' and the axis_state showing blocked. No numeric distance to any crop reference is displayed.","what_dies":"Direct comparison of raw lux against the five corpus PPFD/DLI values (500, 150-200, 140, 200, 11.5) is permanently prohibited regardless of deployment scenario. In a daylit space: the entire plant_light crop-evaluation capability is dead — no distance indicator, no scoring, no ranking. In a sealed LED room without calibration: same as daylit until the one-time reference measurement is performed. The composite score (already rejected by Round 1 consensus) remains dead. What survives: raw lux time-series for human visual environment monitoring and relative change detection within one fixed light source."},"assumptions":["The user's BH1750 decision is final and no quantum sensor will be added as a primary instrument.","The collection_contract's lux_policy and quarantine record all-crops-universal-lux-threshold-q001 are authoritative and binding on schema design.","The conversion_exception path is legitimate and not merely theoretical — if the deployment is truly a sealed LED-only room with no daylight ingress, a one-time side-by-side calibration with a borrowed or rented quantum sensor is feasible and sufficient.","The urban idle space (도심 유휴공간) designation makes daylight ingress the MORE LIKELY scenario, but I do not assume it is certain — some urban idle spaces could be windowless basements or sealed containers.","LED source spectrum is stable over its rated lifetime; the coefficient does not need continuous re-validation, only periodic checks (e.g. annually or when LEDs are replaced)."],"risks":["If the space has any daylight ingress — even indirect through a window — the conversion coefficient is invalid and plant_light is permanently blocked for crop evaluation. This is the highest-probability risk given the urban idle space context.","Even in a sealed LED room, BH1750 accuracy is roughly +/-20% and spectrally dependent; the derived PPFD inherits this uncertainty, making tight distance-to-anchor indicators unreliable at margins.","Operators may perceive the blocked state as a system deficiency rather than a measurement-integrity safeguard, creating pressure to display fake comparisons.","The one-time calibration requires borrowing or renting a quantum sensor — if that is refused, the axis stays blocked indefinitely even in a sealed room.","If LED fixtures are mixed (different models, different spectra, different aging), each fixture-zone combination needs its own calibration row, multiplying the one-time effort."],"cheap_validation":"Borrow or rent any PAR/quantum sensor (e.g. Apogee SQ-520 or LI-COR LI-190R) for one hour. Place it side-by-side with the BH1750 at canopy height under the installed LED fixture with all other light sources blocked. Record 10 paired lux-vs-PPFD readings at varied dimming levels. Compute the mean coefficient (PPFD/lux). If the coefficient's CV across the 10 readings is below 5%, store the mean as the validated conversion coefficient in lux_to_ppfd_calibration. Total time: under 1 hour, total cost: sensor rental fee only. This simultaneously confirms whether daylight ingress exists (coefficient will be unstable if ambient light leaks in).","change_mind_if":"I would upgrade plant_light from 'blocked' to 'evaluable' if and only if: (1) the deployment site is confirmed to be a sealed room with zero daylight ingress AND (2) the one-time quantum-sensor calibration produces a stable coefficient (CV < 5%). I would downgrade my Round 1 language further (from 'too strong' to 'completely wrong') if someone demonstrates a peer-reviewed, sensor-and-source-validated universal lux-to-PPFD conversion that works across LED spectra and daylight mixtures — but no such thing exists in the literature. I would also revise if the user decides to add a quantum sensor as the primary instrument, making BH1750 the secondary channel — but the brief says BH1750 is the decision."}
